{"n": 1, "code": "import numpy as np\nnp.set_printoptions(precision=4, suppress=True, linewidth=160)\nprint(\"shapes:\")\nfor k in sorted(W):\n    print(k, W[k].shape)\nprint(\"\\nLN weights stats:\")\nfor l in range(4):\n    for nm in [f\"ln1_w.{l}\",f\"ln1_b.{l}\",f\"ln2_w.{l}\",f\"ln2_b.{l}\"]:\n        a=W[nm]\n        print(nm, \"mean\",a.mean(),\"std\",a.std(),\"min\",a.min(),\"max\",a.max(),\"norm\",np.linalg.norm(a))\nfor nm in [\"lnf_w\",\"lnf_b\"]:\n    if nm in W:\n        a=W[nm]; print(nm, a.shape, a.mean(),a.std(),a.min(),a.max(),np.linalg.norm(a))\nprint(\"\\nLayer/head norms and singular values:\")\nfor l in range(4):\n    print(\"LAYER\",l)\n    # overall\n    for name in [\"W_q\",\"W_k\",\"W_v\",\"W_o\",\"W_fc\",\"W_proj\"]:\n        a=W[f\"{name}.{l}\"]\n        print(name, \"shape\",a.shape,\"norm\",np.linalg.norm(a),\"mean\",a.mean(),\"std\",a.std())\n    for j in range(6):\n        s=slice(j*64,(j+1)*64)\n        wq=W[f\"W_q.{l}\"][s,:]; wk=W[f\"W_k.{l}\"][s,:]; wv=W[f\"W_v.{l}\"][s,:]\n        wo=W[f\"W_o.{l}\"][:,s]  # in x out? W_o is 384x384, columns head segment\n        # singular vals\n        sq=np.linalg.svd(wq, compute_uv=False); sk=np.linalg.svd(wk, compute_uv=False); sv=np.linalg.svd(wv, compute_uv=False); so=np.linalg.svd(wo, compute_uv=False)\n        # bilinear QK matrix Wq @ Wk.T, out x out\n        A=wq@wk.T\n        sa=np.linalg.svd(A, compute_uv=False)\n        # OV = Wo[:,s] @ Wv? Actually output contribution = att @ v @ W_o^T, head v = h W_v^T; out = att @ h W_v^T W_o[:,s].T? Effective OV from residual input to output: W_v^T? shapes: wv=64x384, wo=384x64, product wv? for each token: v = h @ wv.T (n x64); out = v @ wo.T? code out[:,s] = att @ v[:,s]; then x += out @ W_o.T. out whole n x384, W_o.T 384x384? Wait W_o.l is 384x384, out @ W_o.T. For columns s of out (dims residual?), W_o.T rows dims s? Actually out[:,s] active dims j*hd..; multiplied by W_o.T, where rows of W_o.T correspond dims? out (n,384) @ W_o.T (384,384): contribution to residual = sum_d out[:,d] W_o[:,d]? W_o.T[d, outdim]=W_o[outdim,d]. So columns of W_o correspond input head dims d. Thus effective map input residual h -> v -> output = h @ wv.T @ wo.T? v (n,64)=h (n,384) @ wv.T (384,64). contribution = v @ wo.T (64,384) where wo = W_o[:,s] (384,64). So effective = wv.T @ wo.T? h @ wv.T @ wo.T = h @ (wo @ wv).T? Check (wv.T @ wo.T) shape 384x384. Its rank <=64. Effective output = h @ (wv.T @ wo.T). Equiv h @ (wo @ wv).T? (wo@wv) shape 384x384, transpose same. Wait (wv.T @ wo.T) = (wo @ wv).T. So OV matrix maybe wo @ wv. We'll compute singular values of wo@wv (384x384).\n        OV = wo @ wv  # output x input (resid_out = h @ OV.T?) rank 64\n        sov=np.linalg.svd(OV, compute_uv=False)\n        # QK bilinear can be Wq @ Wk.T -> x Wq^T Wk x'^T? score q k^T = (x wq.T)(x' wk.T)^T = x wq.T wk x'^T. matrix wq.T wk (384x384)\n        QK = wq.T @ wk  # input x input\n        sqk=np.linalg.svd(QK, compute_uv=False)\n        print(f\" H{j}: |q|={np.linalg.norm(wq):.3f} |k|={np.linalg.norm(wk):.3f} |v|={np.linalg.norm(wv):.3f} |o|={np.linalg.norm(wo):.3f} \"\n              f\"svq[0:4]={sq[:4]} svk[0:4]={sk[:4]} svv[0:4]={sv[:4]} svo[0:4]={so[:4]} \"\n              f\"|A|={np.linalg.norm(A):.3f} svA[0:4]={sa[:4]} svOV[0:4]={sov[:4]} svQK[0:4]={sqk[:4]}\")\n", "out": "shapes:\nW_fc.0 (1536, 384)\nW_fc.1 (1536, 384)\nW_fc.2 (1536, 384)\nW_fc.3 (1536, 384)\nW_k.0 (384, 384)\nW_k.1 (384, 384)\nW_k.2 (384, 384)\nW_k.3 (384, 384)\nW_o.0 (384, 384)\nW_o.1 (384, 384)\nW_o.2 (384, 384)\nW_o.3 (384, 384)\nW_proj.0 (384, 1536)\nW_proj.1 (384, 1536)\nW_proj.2 (384, 1536)\nW_proj.3 (384, 1536)\nW_q.0 (384, 384)\nW_q.1 (384, 384)\nW_q.2 (384, 384)\nW_q.3 (384, 384)\nW_v.0 (384, 384)\nW_v.1 (384, 384)\nW_v.2 (384, 384)\nW_v.3 (384, 384)\nln1_b.0 (384,)\nln1_b.1 (384,)\nln1_b.2 (384,)\nln1_b.3 (384,)\nln1_w.0 (384,)\nln1_w.1 (384,)\nln1_w.2 (384,)\nln1_w.3 (384,)\nln2_b.0 (384,)\nln2_b.1 (384,)\nln2_b.2 (384,)\nln2_b.3 (384,)\nln2_w.0 (384,)\n